## #02 — One persisted-receipt validator
Before status, replay or recovery reports a stored receipt, require a dict with
the supported receipt schema, mandatory typed identity/correlation fields and
identity matching the requested delivery, original request and provenance. Missing
request_sha256 is not a wildcard. Correct hash alone cannot excuse mismatched job
or delivery IDs. Refuse malformed/non-object/unsupported receipt data with a clear
structured result and no traceback, never collected success or automatic launch.
Use one helper rather than three divergent checks. Keep legitimate transient
unknown/accepted-not-launched/uncertain states distinguishable from a persisted
receipt; do not demand completed-receipt fields from those transient status forms.
Do not create a signature scheme, approval system or new ledger. The boundary is
accidental/inconsistent stored data in this fixture experiment, not an adversary
rewriting all records. Preserve the read-only behavior of status.

## #03 — Regression and timing evidence
Demonstrate the Prime probe before/after: successful real fixture delivery, remove
its request hash and change its IDs, then fresh-process status. Require refusal
after repair with the receipt bytes preserved. Also cover a correct request hash
with wrong IDs, unsupported schema/non-object data, replay and recover on bad stored
receipts. Prove zero new launches and no source/evidence rewriting on refusal.
Preserve success/status/replay/recovery and current-work/state-change inspection.
Run app integration and entry suites in isolated copies. The integration suite's
inherited-pipe lab test failed at 0.2 seconds in Prime's run; preserve that failure.
If a bounded test-only correction is necessary, may change ONLY lab
tests/test_pass03.py and tests/_driver_pass03.py, with before snapshots and a NEW
pass04 evidence manifest. Keep runtime code, configured dependency hashes, 2-second
cleanup allowance and no-collection invariant unchanged. The chosen test budget
must allow child startup but still catch the original five-second close blockage;
show why, with a regression control. Do not hide timeouts as incomplete-output,
silently skip the mechanism, or widen bounds until an old failure would pass.
If no safe bounded test change is justified, report the failing test and reason
instead of repeating runs until green. No unrelated lab refactor or broad fuzzing.

